`bkpt` (`02 00`, which the vendor compiler emits for its trap builtin)
ends execution with a new error, CoreError::Trap { pc }, the pc left on
the instruction, instead of the unsupported-instruction error it gave
before. fwtest reports it as its own outcome, `trap` (exit code 6), so a
firmware's deliberate trap is told apart from an instruction the
emulator cannot run (the owner's answer, session spec-isa-audit,
2026-10-28). What the chip does on `bkpt` (a debug exception, a halt) is
not established (HARDWARE-SPEC Q-34); `hbkpt`, `swi`, `syscall` and
`trigger` stay unsupported. The crate test bkpt_is_a_trap and the
harness test bkpt_ends_the_run_as_a_trap (tests/images/trap.c) fail
without it.

